      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_45f56fe557ddf80f3a9c9b224ced54c00dd74c19ba4ee957795df9cc4b33d3ae",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The coefficient-side truncation and the moment-side functional equation are not compared term by term. They are embedded in the same meromorphic contour representation, where the target decomposition is controlled by pole locations. Residues are the intermediate objects that preserve the information relevant to the moment while discarding the transform scaffolding.",
