    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6c4a5ef780c2f8e374229b7e19c25a589d7783f20b01937287e326bada2d96a4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The long-polynomial second-moment comparison is completed through a shifted transform bridge: coefficient correlations yield a Fourier-side identity, and Perron inversion, contour rotation, the zeta functional equation, and contour displacement convert it into the two moment-side contributions arising from residues at zero and at the negative combined shift. The unshifted compatibility relation is recovered when the shifts coalesce.",
